WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:03.750
AI agents now answer questions
about company filings.

2
00:00:03.930 --> 00:00:05.610
Some of their answers are wrong.

3
00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:08.920
Here's a replay from
FilingGuard's test set:

4
00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:11.790
a question about Microsoft's
earnings per share.

5
00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:16.360
The agent's real answer
was thirteen sixty-four.

6
00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:19.840
For the test, FilingGuard
swapped in a wrong number:

7
00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:21.190
fourteen thirty-two.

8
00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:24.200
Then it checks the answer
against the filing.

9
00:00:24.410 --> 00:00:27.210
The numbers don't match,
so the answer is blocked.

10
00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:31.210
The real answer passes.

11
00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:35.150
On two hundred ten unseen questions,

12
00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:38.090
it caught ninety-three
percent of planted errors.

13
00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:41.720
But it also blocked nine answers
that were actually correct.

14
00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:43.830
Automatic scoring missed that.

15
00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:45.850
Only a human review found it.

16
00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:49.470
FilingGuard.

17
00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:51.960
Live at filingguard dot vercel dot app.
